@bio:

Benjamin Ory is an FWO Junior Postdoctoral Fellow at KU
Leuven. He received his PhD in musicology from Stanford
University in 2022, and has since served as a Harvard Villa
I Tatti Digital Humanities Fellow and as visiting assistant
professor at Williams College. He is the founder of The
1520s Project (https://1520s-project.org), a digital
library of sixteenth-century music, for which
Ory—together with Jesse Rodin and Craig Sapp—received a
2025 NEH Scholarly Editions and Translations grant. Ory’s
research focuses on sixteenth-century polyphony and the
early history of Renaissance musicology.


@@END: BIO